# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated aggregates. build_data.py rebuilds these wholesale from the
# per-module fragments in app/data/cards/ and app/data/drillsets/, so their
# content is derived, never authored.
#
# Two people working in parallel BOTH regenerate them, so a textual merge
# produces a guaranteed conflict in a multi-megabyte file on every merge --
# and resolving it by hand is meaningless, because the correct answer is
# "regenerate from the fragments" either way.
#
# merge=regen resolves them without conflict markers; the post-merge hook
# then reruns build_data.py so the result is correct rather than just clean.
# Register both, once per clone:  pwsh scripts/setup-collab.ps1
#
# linguist-generated keeps them out of GitHub diffs and language stats.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
app/data/curriculum.json  merge=regen linguist-generated=true
app/data/flashcards.json  merge=regen linguist-generated=true
app/data/drills.json      merge=regen linguist-generated=true
app/data/problems.json    merge=regen linguist-generated=true
app/data/*.js             merge=regen linguist-generated=true
CONTENT-STATUS.md         merge=regen linguist-generated=true
LEARNING-PATH.md          merge=regen linguist-generated=true

# Fragments are the source of truth and are one file per module, so two people
# writing different modules never touch the same file. Normal merge applies.
